@startuml
title Default Remote-First Conflict Handling with ~--resync
start

:Begin remote-first reconciliation with ~--resync;
note right
  Operating mode:
  onedrive ~--sync ~--resync

  ~--resync intentionally discards the previous application
  sync database. The client therefore loses the historical
  last-applied baseline that would normally help prove whether
  an existing local file changed independently.
end note

:Discard previous local sync database state;
:Enumerate current Microsoft OneDrive state and rebuild identity baseline;

if (Online file maps to an existing local pathname?) then (yes)
  :Compare existing local content with online content;
  if (Content already matches?) then (yes)
    :Reconcile timestamp / metadata and rebuild DB record;
    note right
      NO safeBackup is required simply because ~--resync was used.
      If the local and online bytes already match, there is no unique
      local content to preserve and no reason to replace identical data.
    end note
  else (no)
    :Download online replacement into private .partial staging file;
    :Validate downloaded content;
    :Create and verify safeBackup copy of differing local content;
    note right
      LOCAL DATA LOSS PREVENTION

      The previous DB baseline no longer exists, so the client cannot
      use history to prove that the differing local bytes are disposable.
      Conservative preservation protects the local file before the
      authoritative online replacement is committed.
    end note
    if (Preservation fails?) then (yes)
      :Reject replacement; retain local canonical file;
      stop
    endif
    :Recheck canonical stability;
    :Atomically promote validated online replacement;
    :Apply online timestamp and rebuild DB state;
  endif
else (no)
  :Create / download online item normally;
endif

:Run local database/filesystem consistency pass;
:Scan for new local data when uploads are enabled;
note right
  A safeBackup created during rebuild may subsequently be discovered
  as new local data and uploaded unless excluded through skip_file.
end note
:Perform final online true-up where applicable;
stop
@enduml
